# WordPress Plugin Conflict Troubleshooting

## Issue

A WordPress website experienced admin dashboard instability and unexpected layout issues after multiple plugin updates.

---

## Symptoms

- Admin dashboard loading inconsistently
- Visual layout problems inside the WordPress admin panel
- Slow page rendering
- Certain plugin settings pages failing to load correctly

---

## Troubleshooting Steps

1. Reviewed recently updated plugins
2. Enabled troubleshooting workflow using plugin isolation techniques
3. Temporarily switched to a default WordPress theme
4. Disabled plugins individually to identify the conflicting plugin
5. Reviewed browser console logs for JavaScript-related issues
6. Tested dashboard functionality after each plugin change

---

## Root Cause

A conflict between two plugins loading overlapping admin-side JavaScript assets caused dashboard instability and rendering issues.

---

## Resolution

- Disabled the conflicting plugin temporarily
- Updated plugin configuration settings
- Re-enabled plugins incrementally after validation
- Confirmed stable admin dashboard performance

---

## Prevention

- Test plugin updates in staging environments before deployment
- Avoid redundant plugins with overlapping functionality
- Monitor admin-side JavaScript errors after plugin installations